        "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <memory>\n#include <vector>\n\nclass FastInput {\n    unsigned char buffer_[1 << 16];\n    std::size_t position_ = 0;\n    std::size_t length_ = 0;\n\n    int next_char() {\n        if (position_ == length_) {\n            length_ = std::fread(buffer_, 1, sizeof(buffer_), stdin);\n            position_ = 0;\n            if (length_ == 0) return EOF;\n        }\n        return buffer_[position_++];\n    }\n\npublic:\n    bool read_int(int& result) {\n        int c;\n        do {\n            c = next_char();\n            if (c == EOF) return false;\n        } while (c <= ' ');\n\n        const bool negative = c == '-';\n        if (c == '-' || c == '+') c = next_char();\n        unsigned int value = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            value = value * 10u + static_cast<unsigned int>(c - '0');\n            c = next_char();\n        }\n        result = negative\n            ? static_cast<int>(-static_cast<std::int64_t>(value))\n            : static_cast<int>(value);\n        return true;\n    }\n};\n\nstatic std::int64_t maximum_horizontal_window(\n    const std::int64_t* columns, int n, int s) {\n    std::int64_t sum = 0;\n    for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) sum += columns[j];\n    std::int64_t best = sum;\n    for (int j = s; j < n; ++j) {\n        sum += columns[j] - columns[j - s];\n        if (sum > best) best = sum;\n    }\n    return best;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    FastInput input;\n    int n, s;\n    if (!input.read_int(n) || !input.read_int(s)) return 0;\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    const int outgoing_rows = n - s;\n    const int history_rows = std::min(s, outgoing_rows);\n    const std::size_t stride = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> history(\n        new int[stride * static_cast<std::size_t>(history_rows)]);\n    std::vector<std::int64_t> columns(n, 0);\n\n    // Only rows that can leave a valid window need to be retained.\n    for (int row = 0; row < history_rows; ++row) {\n        int* saved = history.get() + static_cast<std::size_t>(row) * stride;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int value;\n            input.read_int(value);\n            saved[j] = value;\n            columns[j] += value;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int row = history_rows; row < s; ++row) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int value;\n            input.read_int(value);\n            columns[j] += value;\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::int64_t best = maximum_horizontal_window(columns.data(), n, s);\n    int slot = 0;\n    for (int row = s; row < n; ++row) {\n        int* outgoing = history.get() + static_cast<std::size_t>(slot) * stride;\n        if (row < outgoing_rows) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                int value;\n                input.read_int(value);\n                columns[j] += static_cast<std::int64_t>(value) - outgoing[j];\n                outgoing[j] = value;\n            }\n        } else {\n            // These incoming rows will never leave a subsequent window.\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                int value;\n                input.read_int(value);\n                columns[j] += static_cast<std::int64_t>(value) - outgoing[j];\n            }\n        }\n        const std::int64_t candidate =\n            maximum_horizontal_window(columns.data(), n, s);\n        if (candidate > best) best = candidate;\n        if (++slot == history_rows) slot = 0;\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", static_cast<long long>(best));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Streaming raw outgoing rows through a compact FIFO and maintaining contiguous column sums should eliminate strided accesses and reduce computation to O(N²), with history limited to N*min(S,N-S) integers.",
